From: MedyMa <75345465+MedyMa@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: aquantia: preserve SFP module startup state

The additional vendor POR reset in aqr107_probe also runs on PHYs inside
SFP modules. Those PHYs are provisioned by their module controller, and
resetting them can discard that state before phylink attaches the module.
Skip this board-level reset for SFP PHYs, as in the 24.10 driver, while
keeping the existing reset sequence for non-SFP PHYs. Keep the standard
firmware-readiness wait and the remaining probe and cleanup paths intact.

Signed-off-by: MedyMa <75345465+MedyMa@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_main.c
@@ -981,7 +981,9 @@ static int aqr107_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
 	if (!phydev->priv)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
-	aqr107_phy_reset(phydev);
+	/* Preserve provisioning owned by the SFP module controller. */
+	if (!phydev->is_on_sfp_module)
+		aqr107_phy_reset(phydev);
 
 	ret = aqr_firmware_load(phydev);
 	if (ret)
